GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Definition in section 17`)
`s 17: the definition printed for the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN entry IS A `Definition in section 17` YIELD entry's `term as printed` EQUALS term) `definitions in section 17`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST x

@ref Section 17, Definitions (lines 233 to 415)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE (`How a term is defined in section 17`)
`s 17: how the term is defined` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 17: the definition printed for the term` term
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entry THEN JUST (entry's `how defined`)

@ref Section 17, Definitions (lines 233 to 415)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 17: the provision of this Act at which the definition of the term points` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 17: the definition printed for the term` term
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entry THEN entry's `provision of this Act pointed at`

@ref Section 17, Definitions (lines 233 to 415)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 17: the other law at which the definition of the term points` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 17: the definition printed for the term` term
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entry THEN entry's `other law pointed at`

@ref Section 17, Definitions (lines 233 to 415)
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 17: the provision of the other law at which the definition of the term points` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 17: the definition printed for the term` term
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST entry THEN entry's `provision of the other law pointed at`

§ `Definitions that decide a case from facts`

-- Each function below follows one definition in section 17.
-- A "means" definition is closed, so a case outside it is JUST FALSE; an "includes" definition is open, so a case outside what it lists is NOTHING.
-- Facts borrowed from another law (what the Banking Act 1959 permits, who is registered under a national law) are inputs.

-- Adult means an individual who is at least 18 years old.  A person has attained an age on the anniversary of the birth (section 30).
-- src:243 | adult means an individual who is at least 18 years old.
@ref s 17 "adult" (src:243)
GIVEN `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "adult": the person is an adult on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 30(1): the person has attained the age on` `the date of birth` 18 `the day asked about`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN JUST (`the person is an individual` AND attained)

-- Infant means a person who has not attained the age of 18 years.
-- src:328 | infant means a person who has not attained the age of 18 years.
@ref s 17 "infant" (src:328)
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "infant": the person is an infant on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 30(1): the person has attained the age on` `the date of birth` 18 `the day asked about`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST attained THEN JUST (NOT attained)

-- Individual means a natural person.
-- src:327 | individual means a natural person.
@ref s 17 "individual" (src:327)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "individual": the person is an individual` MEANS JUST `the person is a natural person`

DECLARE `Entity asked about in section 17` IS ONE OF
    `an entity that is a body politic`
    `an entity that is a body corporate`
    `an entity that is a natural person`
    `an entity of some other kind`

-- Person includes a body politic and a body corporate.
-- src:369 | person includes a body politic and a body corporate.
@ref s 17 "person" (src:369)
GIVEN entity IS A `Entity asked about in section 17`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "person": the entity is within a person` MEANS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `an entity that is a body politic` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an entity that is a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Party includes a body politic and a body corporate.
-- src:367 | party includes a body politic and a body corporate.
@ref s 17 "party" (src:367)
GIVEN entity IS A `Entity asked about in section 17`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "party": the entity is within a party` MEANS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `an entity that is a body politic` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an entity that is a body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Gazette notice means a notice published in the Gazette.
-- src:311 | Gazette notice means a notice published in the Gazette.
@ref s 17 "Gazette notice" (src:311)
GIVEN `it is a notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "Gazette notice": the thing is a Gazette notice` MEANS JUST (`it is a notice` AND `it is published in the Gazette`)

-- Gazette, Government Gazette, Northern Territory Government Gazette or Gazette of the Northern Territory means the Government Gazette of the Territory.
-- src:310 | Gazette, Government Gazette, Northern Territory Government Gazette or Gazette of the Northern Territory means the Government Gazette of the Territory.
@ref s 17 "Gazette" (src:310)
GIVEN expression IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 17 "Gazette": what the expression means` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN known YIELD known EQUALS expression) (LIST "Gazette", "Government Gazette", "Northern Territory Government Gazette", "Gazette of the Northern Territory")
    THEN JUST "the Government Gazette of the Territory"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Proclamation means proclamation by the Administrator published in the Gazette.
-- src:374 | proclamation means proclamation by the Administrator published in the Gazette.
@ref s 17 "proclamation" (src:374)
GIVEN `it is a proclamation by the Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "proclamation": the thing is a proclamation` MEANS JUST (`it is a proclamation by the Administrator` AND `it is published in the Gazette`)

-- Notified in the Gazette, in relation to an instrument, means that notification of the making of the instrument and four items of information is published in the Gazette.
-- src:356 | notified in the Gazette, in relation to an instrument, means that notification of the making of the instrument and the following information is published in the Gazette:
-- src:357 | (a) the title of the Act under which the instrument is published;
-- src:358 | (b) the provision of the Act under which the instrument is required to be published that provides the power for the making of the instrument;
-- src:359 | (c) the title of the instrument;
-- src:360 | (d) the date of making of the instrument.
@ref s 17 "notified in the Gazette" (src:356-360)
GIVEN `notification of the making of the instrument is published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification gives the title of the Act under which the instrument is published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification gives the provision of that Act that provides the power for the making of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification gives the title of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification gives the date of making of the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "notified in the Gazette": the instrument is notified in the Gazette` MEANS
    JUST (`notification of the making of the instrument is published in the Gazette`
          AND `the notification gives the title of the Act under which the instrument is published`
          AND `the notification gives the provision of that Act that provides the power for the making of the instrument`
          AND `the notification gives the title of the instrument`
          AND `the notification gives the date of making of the instrument`)

-- Committed for trial, in relation to a person, means committed into custody with a view to being tried before a judge and jury, or granted bail under the Bail Act 1982 to appear and be tried before a judge and jury.
-- src:275 | committed for trial, in relation to a person, means:
-- src:276 | (a) committed into the custody of the Commissioner of Correctional Services, or the Chief Executive Officer (as defined in section 19 of the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993) of the Agency responsible for youth justice, with a view to being tried before a judge and jury; or
-- src:277 | (b) granted bail under the Bail Act 1982 to appear and be tried before a judge and jury.
@ref s 17 "committed for trial" (src:275-277)
GIVEN `the person is committed into the custody of the Commissioner of Correctional Services, or of the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency responsible for youth justice, with a view to being tried before a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is granted bail under the Bail Act 1982 to appear and be tried before a judge and jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "committed for trial": the person is committed for trial` MEANS
    JUST (`the person is committed into the custody of the Commissioner of Correctional Services, or of the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency responsible for youth justice, with a view to being tried before a judge and jury`
          OR `the person is granted bail under the Bail Act 1982 to appear and be tried before a judge and jury`)

DECLARE `Thing asked about under the definition of document` IS ONE OF
    `paper or other material on which there is writing`
    `a map, plan, drawing or photograph`
    `paper or other material on which there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them`
    `an article or material from which sounds, images or writings are capable of being reproduced`
    `an article on which information has been stored or recorded, either mechanically or electronically`
    `any other record or information`
    `a copy, reproduction or duplicate, or part of a copy, reproduction or duplicate, of one of these things`
    `a thing of some other kind`

-- Document includes any of, or part of any of, the six things listed in paragraph (a), and a copy, reproduction or duplicate of such a thing.
-- src:289 | document includes:
-- src:290 | (a) any of, or part of any of, the following things:
-- src:291 | (i) paper or other material on which there is writing;
-- src:292 | (ii) a map, plan, drawing or photograph;
-- src:293 | (iii) paper or other material on which there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them;
-- src:294 | (iv) an article or any material from which sounds, images or writings are capable of being reproduced with or without the aid of another article or device;
-- src:295 | (v) an article on which information has been stored or recorded, either mechanically or electronically;
-- src:296 | (vi) any other record or information; and
-- src:297 | (b) a copy, reproduction or duplicate, or part of a copy, reproduction or duplicate, of a thing mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 17 "document" (src:289-297)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing asked about under the definition of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "document": the thing is within a document` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `a thing of some other kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Place asked about under the definition of public place` IS ONE OF
    `a place to which free access is permitted to the public with the express or tacit consent of the owner or occupier`
    `a place to which the public are admitted on payment of money`
    `a road, street, footway, court, alley or thoroughfare that the public are allowed to use, even if on private property`
    `a place of some other kind`

-- Public place includes the three kinds of place listed.
-- src:376 | public place includes the following:
-- src:377 | (a) a place to which free access is permitted to the public with the express or tacit consent of the owner or occupier of the place;
-- src:378 | (b) a place to which the public are admitted on payment of money;
-- src:379 | (c) a road, street, footway, court, alley or thoroughfare that the public are allowed to use, even if the road, street, footway, court, alley or thoroughfare is on private property.
@ref s 17 "public place" (src:376-379)
GIVEN place IS A `Place asked about under the definition of public place`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "public place": the place is within a public place` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `a place of some other kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Indictable offence means an offence that is indictable under section 3(2) of the Criminal Code, or an act or omission outside the Territory that would be so indictable if committed in the Territory.
-- src:323 | indictable offence means:
-- src:324 | (a) an offence that is an indictable offence under section 3(2) of the Criminal Code; or
-- src:325 | (b) an act or omission committed outside the Territory that would be an indictable offence under paragraph (a) if it were committed in the Territory.
@ref s 17 "indictable offence" (src:323-325)
GIVEN `it is an offence that is an indictable offence under section 3(2) of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an act or omission committed outside the Territory that would be an indictable offence under that section if it were committed in the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "indictable offence": the offence is an indictable offence` MEANS
    JUST (`it is an offence that is an indictable offence under section 3(2) of the Criminal Code`
          OR `it is an act or omission committed outside the Territory that would be an indictable offence under that section if it were committed in the Territory`)

-- Law of the Territory means an Act, an instrument of a legislative character, an existing law of the Territory within section 57 of the Self-Government Act that is neither, or the common law.
-- src:333 | law of the Territory means:
-- src:334 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:335 | (b) an instrument of a legislative character; or
-- src:336 | (c) an existing law of the Territory within the meaning of section 57 of the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth) that is not a law mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b); or
-- src:337 | (d) the common law.
@ref s 17 "law of the Territory" (src:333-337)
GIVEN `it is an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument of a legislative character` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an existing law of the Territory within the meaning of section 57 of the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the common law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "law of the Territory": the thing is a law of the Territory` MEANS
    JUST (`it is an Act` OR `it is an instrument of a legislative character` OR `it is an existing law of the Territory within the meaning of section 57 of the Northern Territory (Self-Government) Act 1978 (Cth)` OR `it is the common law`)

-- Legislation website means the website at legislation.nt.gov.au maintained by the Agency, or an alternative website authorised in writing by the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency.
-- src:340 | legislation website means:
-- src:341 | (a) the website with the address legislation.nt.gov.au maintained by the Agency; or
-- src:342 | (b) an alternative website authorised in writing by the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency.
@ref s 17 "legislation website" (src:340-342)
GIVEN `it is the website with the address legislation.nt.gov.au maintained by the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an alternative website authorised in writing by the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "legislation website": the website is the legislation website` MEANS
    JUST (`it is the website with the address legislation.nt.gov.au maintained by the Agency` OR `it is an alternative website authorised in writing by the Chief Executive Officer of the Agency`)

-- Medical practitioner means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the medical profession (other than as a student).
-- src:349 | medical practitioner means a person registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the medical profession (other than as a student).
@ref s 17 "medical practitioner" (src:349)
GIVEN `the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the medical profession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registration is as a student` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "medical practitioner": the person is a medical practitioner` MEANS
    JUST (`the person is registered under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law to practise in the medical profession` AND (NOT `the registration is as a student`))

-- Subordinate legislation means regulations, rules or by-laws to which section 63 or 63A applies, or a statutory instrument that under an Act is an instrument to which section 63 or 63A applies.
-- src:395 | subordinate legislation means:
-- src:396 | (a) regulations, rules or by-laws to which section 63 or 63A applies; or
-- src:397 | (b) a statutory instrument that, under an Act, is an instrument to which section 63 or 63A applies.
@ref s 17 "subordinate legislation" (src:395-397)
GIVEN `they are regulations, rules or by-laws to which section 63 or 63A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a statutory instrument that, under an Act, is an instrument to which section 63 or 63A applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "subordinate legislation": the instrument is subordinate legislation` MEANS
    JUST (`they are regulations, rules or by-laws to which section 63 or 63A applies` OR `it is a statutory instrument that, under an Act, is an instrument to which section 63 or 63A applies`)

-- Statutory corporation means a corporation, commission or authority incorporated by name for a public purpose by a law of the Territory, but does not include a local government council.
-- src:390 | statutory corporation means a corporation, commission or authority incorporated by name for a public purpose by a law of the Territory, but does not include a local government council.
@ref s 17 "statutory corporation" (src:390)
GIVEN `it is a corporation, commission or authority incorporated by name for a public purpose by a law of the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a local government council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "statutory corporation": the body is a statutory corporation` MEANS
    JUST (`it is a corporation, commission or authority incorporated by name for a public purpose by a law of the Territory` AND (NOT `it is a local government council`))

-- Instrument of a legislative or administrative character includes regulations, rules, by-laws, orders, determinations, proclamations, awards, documents and authorities made, granted or issued under a power conferred by an Act.
-- src:330 | instrument of a legislative or administrative character includes regulations, rules, by-laws, orders, determinations, proclamations, awards, documents and authorities made, granted or issued under a power conferred by an Act.
@ref s 17 "instrument of a legislative or administrative character" (src:330)
GIVEN kind IS A STRING
      `it is made, granted or issued under a power conferred by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "instrument of a legislative or administrative character": the thing is within such an instrument` MEANS
    IF   any (GIVEN known YIELD known EQUALS kind) (LIST "regulations", "rules", "by-laws", "orders", "determinations", "proclamations", "awards", "documents", "authorities")
         AND `it is made, granted or issued under a power conferred by an Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Statutory instrument means an instrument of a legislative or administrative character.
-- src:392 | statutory instrument means an instrument of a legislative or administrative character.
@ref s 17 "statutory instrument" (src:392)
GIVEN `it is an instrument of a legislative or administrative character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "statutory instrument": the thing is a statutory instrument` MEANS JUST `it is an instrument of a legislative or administrative character`

-- Bank means an ADI permitted under the Banking Act 1959 to assume or use the word bank, banker or banking, or another word of like import.
-- src:253 | bank means an ADI that is permitted under the Banking Act 1959 (Cth) to assume or use:
-- src:254 | (a) the word bank, banker or banking; or
-- src:255 | (b) any other word (whether or not in English) that is of like import to a word mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 17 "bank" (src:253-255)
GIVEN `it is an ADI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is permitted under the Banking Act 1959 (Cth) to assume or use the word bank, banker or banking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is permitted under that Act to assume or use another word of like import` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "bank": the ADI is a bank` MEANS
    JUST (`it is an ADI` AND (`it is permitted under the Banking Act 1959 (Cth) to assume or use the word bank, banker or banking` OR `it is permitted under that Act to assume or use another word of like import`))

-- Bank cheque or banker's cheque means a cheque that an ADI draws on itself.
-- src:256 | bank cheque or banker's cheque means a cheque that an ADI draws on itself.
@ref s 17 "bank cheque" (src:256)
GIVEN `it is a cheque` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an ADI draws it on itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "bank cheque": the cheque is a bank cheque or banker's cheque` MEANS JUST (`it is a cheque` AND `an ADI draws it on itself`)

-- Building society means an ADI permitted under the Banking Act 1959 to assume or use the expression building society, or another expression of like import.
-- src:257 | building society means an ADI that is permitted under the Banking Act 1959 (Cth) to assume or use:
-- src:258 | (a) the expression building society; or
-- src:259 | (b) any other expression (whether or not in English) that is of like import to the expression mentioned in paragraph (a).
@ref s 17 "building society" (src:257-259)
GIVEN `it is an ADI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is permitted under the Banking Act 1959 (Cth) to assume or use the expression building society` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is permitted under that Act to assume or use another expression of like import` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "building society": the ADI is a building society` MEANS
    JUST (`it is an ADI` AND (`it is permitted under the Banking Act 1959 (Cth) to assume or use the expression building society` OR `it is permitted under that Act to assume or use another expression of like import`))

-- External territory means a Territory, other than the Australian Capital Territory, the Jervis Bay Territory or the Northern Territory, for whose government as a Territory a Commonwealth Act makes provision.
-- src:302 | external territory means a Territory, other than the Australian Capital Territory, the Jervis Bay Territory or the Northern Territory, for the government of which as a Territory provision is made by a Commonwealth Act.
@ref s 17 "external territory" (src:302)
GIVEN `the name of the Territory` IS A STRING
      `a Commonwealth Act makes provision for its government as a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "external territory": the Territory is an external territory` MEANS
    JUST ((NOT (any (GIVEN excluded YIELD excluded EQUALS `the name of the Territory`) (LIST "Australian Capital Territory", "Jervis Bay Territory", "Northern Territory")))
          AND `a Commonwealth Act makes provision for its government as a Territory`)

-- Contravene includes fail to comply with.
-- src:281 | contravene includes fail to comply with.
@ref s 17 "contravene" (src:281)
GIVEN `it is a failure to comply with the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17 "contravene": the thing is within a contravention` MEANS IF `it is a failure to comply with the provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Function includes duty.
-- src:309 | function includes duty.
@ref s 17 "function" (src:309)
GIVEN `it is a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
